@baseUrl = https://localhost:8010/camplib/v1

### ============================================================
### Books API
### Seed-based manual API test
### ============================================================
###
### Important:
### The database should be deleted/reset before running this file.
### This file rebuilds the required Catalog seed data through the public API.
###
### Seed.cs is the source of the stable ids.
### The .http file creates the seed data through HTTP.
###
### Current Catalog simplification:
### - There is no Author aggregate.
### - There are no /authors endpoints.
### - There is no /books/{bookId}/authors endpoint.
### - Author names are stored directly in Book.AuthorsText.
### - AuthorLastName search parses AuthorsText at commas and uses the
###   last whitespace-separated token of each author as lastname.
### ============================================================

@book1Id = 00000001-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@book2Id = 00000002-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@book3Id = 00000003-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@book4Id = 00000004-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

@bookItem1Id = 00000001-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@bookItem2Id = 00000002-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@bookItem3Id = 00000003-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@bookItem4Id = 00000004-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@bookItem5Id = 00000005-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@bookItem6Id = 00000006-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

@book1Isbn = 9780132350884
@book2Isbn = 9780321125217
@book3Isbn = 9780201485677
@book4Isbn = 9780201633610

@unknownBookId = 00000999-0000-0000-0000-000000000000


### 1. Create seed books =======================================================
### Book_Post
### BookItem_Post


### Verify seed books =======================================================

### Get seed book 1: Clean Code
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/{{book1Id}}
Accept: application/json

### Get seed book 2: Domain-Driven Design
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/{{book2Id}}
Accept: application/json

### Get seed book 3: Refactoring
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/{{book3Id}}
Accept: application/json

### Get seed book 4: Design Patterns
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/{{book4Id}}
Accept: application/json

### Get all active books
GET {{baseUrl}}/books
Accept: application/json


### Search books by title ===================================================

### Search Clean Code by title
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/search?searchField=Title&searchText=Clean
Accept: application/json

### Search Domain-Driven Design by title
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/search?searchField=Title&searchText=Domain
Accept: application/json

### Search Refactoring by title
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/search?searchField=Title&searchText=Refactoring
Accept: application/json

### Search Design Patterns by title
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/search?searchField=Title&searchText=Patterns
Accept: application/json

### Search with no expected result
### Expected: 200 OK with empty list
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/search?searchField=Title&searchText=NoSuchBook
Accept: application/json


### Search books by ISBN ====================================================

### Search Clean Code by ISBN
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/search?searchField=Isbn&searchText={{book1Isbn}}
Accept: application/json

### Search Domain-Driven Design by ISBN
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/search?searchField=Isbn&searchText={{book2Isbn}}
Accept: application/json

### Search Refactoring by ISBN
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/search?searchField=Isbn&searchText={{book3Isbn}}
Accept: application/json

### Search Design Patterns by ISBN
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/search?searchField=Isbn&searchText={{book4Isbn}}
Accept: application/json


### 6. Search books by author lastname ========================================

### Search books by author lastname Martin
### Expected: Clean Code only.
### Reason: "Robert C. Martin" has lastname Martin.
### "Martin Fowler" must not match because Martin is the firstname there.
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/search?searchField=AuthorLastName&searchText=Martin
Accept: application/json


### Search books by author lastname Evans
### Expected: Domain-Driven Design
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/search?searchField=AuthorLastName&searchText=Evans
Accept: application/json


### Search books by author lastname Fowler
### Expected: Refactoring
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/search?searchField=AuthorLastName&searchText=Fowler
Accept: application/json


### Search books by author lastname Beck
### Expected: Refactoring
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/search?searchField=AuthorLastName&searchText=Beck
Accept: application/json


### Search books by author lastname Gamma
### Expected: Design Patterns
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/search?searchField=AuthorLastName&searchText=Gamma
Accept: application/json


### Search books by author lastname Helm
### Expected: Design Patterns
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/search?searchField=AuthorLastName&searchText=Helm
Accept: application/json


### Search books by author lastname Johnson
### Expected: Design Patterns
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/search?searchField=AuthorLastName&searchText=Johnson
Accept: application/json


### Search books by author lastname Vlissides
### Expected: Design Patterns
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/search?searchField=AuthorLastName&searchText=Vlissides
Accept: application/json


### 7. Negative read and search tests =========================================

### Get unknown book by id
### Expected: 404 Not Found
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/{{unknownBookId}}
Accept: application/json


### Search books with invalid search field
### Expected: 400 Bad Request
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/search?searchField=Unknown&searchText=Clean
Accept: application/json


### Search books with empty search text
### Expected: 200 OK with empty list
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/search?searchField=Title&searchText=
Accept: application/json


### 8. Conflict tests using seed data =========================================

### Create book with existing seed id and existing seed ISBN
### Expected: 409 Conflict
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "authorsText": "Robert C. Martin",
  "title": "Clean Code",
  "subtitle": "A Handbook of Agile Software Craftsmanship",
  "isbn": "{{book1Isbn}}",
  "id": "{{book1Id}}"
}


### Create book with existing seed ISBN and no explicit id
### Expected: 409 Conflict
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "authorsText": "Duplicate Author",
  "title": "Duplicate ISBN Book",
  "subtitle": null,
  "isbn": "{{book2Isbn}}",
  "id": null
}


### Add duplicate inventory number
### Seed already contains CL-BOOK-0001
### Expected: 409 Conflict
POST {{baseUrl}}/books/{{book1Id}}/items
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "inventoryNumber": "CL-BOOK-0001",
  "id": null
}


### 9. Validation tests ========================================================

### Create book with invalid ISBN
### Expected: 400 Bad Request
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "authorsText": "Invalid Author",
  "title": "Invalid ISBN Book",
  "subtitle": null,
  "isbn": "invalid-isbn",
  "id": null
}


### Create book with missing title
### Expected: 400 Bad Request
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "authorsText": "Valid Author",
  "title": "",
  "subtitle": null,
  "isbn": "9780131103627",
  "id": null
}


### Create book with missing authorsText
### Expected: 400 Bad Request
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "authorsText": "",
  "title": "Book Without Authors",
  "subtitle": null,
  "isbn": "9780201616224",
  "id": null
}


### Create book with only comma-separated empty authors
### Expected: 400 Bad Request
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "authorsText": "  ,  ,  ",
  "title": "Book Without Valid Authors",
  "subtitle": null,
  "isbn": "9780137081073",
  "id": null
}


### Add BookItem with missing inventory number
### Expected: 400 Bad Request
POST {{baseUrl}}/books/{{book1Id}}/items
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "inventoryNumber": "",
  "id": null
}


### Add BookItem to unknown book
### Expected: 404 Not Found
POST {{baseUrl}}/books/{{unknownBookId}}/items
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "inventoryNumber": "CL-BOOK-9999",
  "id": null
}


### 10. Destructive deactivation tests ========================================
### Run these last.
### They change the database state.


### Deactivate seed book 4: Design Patterns
### Expected: 200 OK
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/books/{{book4Id}}/deactivate
Accept: application/json


### Get deactivated seed book 4
### Expected: 404 Not Found
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/{{book4Id}}
Accept: application/json


### Search deactivated seed book by title
### Expected: 200 OK without Design Patterns
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/search?searchField=Title&searchText=Patterns
Accept: application/json


### Search deactivated seed book by author lastname
### Expected: 200 OK without Design Patterns
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/search?searchField=AuthorLastName&searchText=Gamma
Accept: application/json


### Get all active books after deactivation
### Expected: 200 OK without Design Patterns
GET {{baseUrl}}/books
Accept: application/json


### Deactivate unknown book
### Expected: 404 Not Found
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/books/{{unknownBookId}}/deactivate
Accept: application/json
